WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.400
Noise, and error correction.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.235
Why has nothing commercially useful run yet?

3
00:00:05.235 --> 00:00:07.367
Because every gate is slightly wrong.

4
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:12.300
We are in the NISQ era: noisy, intermediate scale quantum.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.867
Machines have tens to a few thousand physical qubits.

6
00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:19.633
And an error rate near one in a thousand per two qubit gate.

7
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:22.133
Why does that kill us?

8
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.200
Errors multiply across the circuit.

9
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:31.267
With a zero point one percent error per gate, a circuit of a few thousand gates is almost guaranteed to be wrong.

10
00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.267
Noise comes from three places.

11
00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:41.333
Decoherence: qubits lose their state in microseconds to milliseconds, so everything must finish in that window.

12
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:45.733
Gate infidelity: each operation is a slightly wrong rotation.

13
00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.200
And reading a qubit is wrong about one percent of the time.

14
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.133
The escape is error correction.

15
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:55.967
We spread one logical qubit across many physical qubits.

16
00:00:56.267 --> 00:01:00.967
We detect errors without measuring, and so without destroying, the encoded state.

17
00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:03.367
The surface code is the leading scheme.

18
00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:07.031
Done well, the result is one stable logical qubit.

19
00:01:07.031 --> 00:01:10.800
Hardware is now below the roughly one percent threshold.

20
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.367
But the cost is huge.

21
00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:17.194
About a thousand physical qubits for every logical one.

22
00:01:17.194 --> 00:01:21.233
The real roadmap is not more qubits, it is more logical qubits.

23
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:26.633
The one quantum skill that pays today is post quantum cryptography.

24
00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:29.533
Adversaries record encrypted traffic now.

25
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:36.000
They decrypt it when a capable machine exists, which matters for data that must stay secret ten years or more.

26
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:45.433
NIST standardized ML-KEM and ML-DSA in 2024, so migration is ordinary engineering with scarce vocabulary.

27
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:47.385
Let's recap.

28
00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:51.267
Today's machines have about zero point one percent gate error.

29
00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.067
Errors compound with depth.

30
00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:57.833
Error correction costs around a thousand physical qubits per logical one.

31
00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.508
And post quantum migration is the skill in demand now.

32
00:02:01.508 --> 00:02:03.633
Next up: quantum machine learning.
